# tests/mpx7-mux.d/screen.rows — px125: what the console draws, answers and sends for a multiplexer's
# client (tests/mpx7-mux.d/screen.py's lines, `ROW NAME<TAB>VERDICT`), measured on PAX under QEMU. A
# verdict says how the case compares with xterm (cases.py writes xterm's screen for each case from the
# XTerm Control Sequences document): `xterm's`, or `not xterm's` with the first row that differs; an
# SGR sample's colours and how they stand to xterm's rendition; a glyph line's count; a query's
# answer; a key's bytes. notes/px125-multiplexer-readiness.md section B reads them.
#
# px125's two fixes: Ctrl-Space sends NUL (kernel/console), and the box-drawing block, the arrows and
# the powerline separators are drawn (font/extent.txt). Every other line is the console as it was.
B1 b1-alt-on	xterm's
B1 b1-alt-off	xterm's
B1 b1-alt-47	not xterm's (row 0: 'mainalt' want 'main')
B1 b1-decsc	xterm's
B1 b1-scosc	not xterm's (row 0: 'abc' want 'abcd')
